            <ArticleTitle>Therapeutic repositioning of a Gianturco-Roubin II coronary stent after initial deployment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>57-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Movement of coronary stents after deployment can produce complications. We report a case of stent migration that led to stent coverage of a distal dissection, obviating the need for placement of a second stent. In this case, stent movement was therapeutic.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
